<DocLayout
  title="Troubleshooting"
  description="Resolve rob-mcp boot failures, RPC chain mismatch, HTTP 402 and 413 responses, free-tier exhaustion, unavailable pools, and oracle safety errors."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Typed failures, concrete fixes</p><h1>Troubleshooting</h1>
  <h2>RPC chain mismatch</h2>
  <p>
    The configured RPC returned a chain ID different from its <code>RPC_URL_&lt;chainId&gt;</code> name.
    Point the variable to the correct enabled EVM chain and restart.
  </p>
  <h2>HTTP 402</h2>
  <p>
    The deployment’s free allowance is exhausted. Use an x402-aware client configured for the
    network in the challenge; do not reuse a settled payment authorization.
  </p>
  <h2>HTTP 413</h2>
  <p>
    The declared or streamed POST body exceeds the deployment’s configured cap. Submit only the
    canonical tool input fields.
  </p>
  <h2><code>SEQUENCER_STATUS_UNAVAILABLE</code></h2>
  <p>
    The required official L2 liveness source is unavailable. This is expected for current Robinhood
    Chain price-bearing reads while O-8 remains open; there is no caller bypass.
  </p>
  <h2><code>NO_VERIFIED_POOL</code></h2>
  <p>
    No verified pool is registered for the requested token and venue. Discovery can still succeed
    and liquidity can return an empty venues list.
  </p>
  <h2>Stale or paused oracle</h2>
  <p>
    The reference source failed freshness or safety checks. Wait for the upstream source to recover;
    rob-mcp intentionally returns no price-bearing result.
  </p>
  <h2>Facilitator unavailable</h2>
  <p>
    Payment verification or settlement could not complete. Keep the payment authorization private to
    your client and retry after the configured facilitator recovers.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
